#### 🟢 **2026-08-27 (night, later) — `D-S11-2` WAS RAISED AND CLOSED THE SAME DAY. `G9.15` PUTS THE MUTATION DETECTOR BACK, AT THE SOURCE'S OWN 200 l/day, AND IT WAS SEEN FAILING BEFORE IT WAS TRUSTED.**

🟢 **The author ruled the repair within hours of the previous entry raising it:** score the per-**dwelling** daily volume against Jordan & Vajen's own **200 l/day, ±10 %**. That is now **`G9.15`** in `tools/4thJ_gates_step9.py`, and `tools/4thJ_step9_selftest.py`'s registered table hands `scale_dhw_by_2` to it. 🔴 **`G9.7` and `G11.7` are still `INFO` and `G9_7_BAND_L_PER_PERSON_DAY` is still `(30.0, 50.0)`** — nothing here rehabilitates the per-person band, and nothing here is a threshold that moved.

🟢 **1. Seen failing before it was trusted, at the gate and in the registered battery.** Shipped tables → **PASS** at stock means `200.79 / 201.01 / 199.47` l/dwelling/day (`+0.4 / +0.5 / −0.3 %`). Every `dhw_*` column doubled in a copy → **FAIL** at `401.58 / 402.03 / 398.93` (`+100.8 / +101.0 / +99.5 %`). 🟢 **And the registered battery says the same thing as the probe:** re-run the same day, **13 HIT / 0 MISS / 2 already-failing, null perturbation moved nothing, COVERAGE CLAUSE PASS** (308.1 s, 25 households, fold `es`), with `scale_dhw_by_2` a **HIT on `G9.15`** — *"fell and its clean set stayed clean"*. ⚪ The shipped counts were `12 / 0 / 3`; one already-failing gate became an `INFO` classification and one genuine hit took its place. ⚪ **Two independent paths agree on the scored figure, so the arm is not a constant echoed back:** the manifest's `stock_dhw_l_per_dwelling_day`, integrated from the stock time series by a different branch of the trigger, reads `200.792 / 201.015 / 199.466` against the table means `200.79 / 201.01 / 199.47`, and the trigger's own comment records that this comparison already caught a units error once. ⚪ Step 9 now reads **`16 PASS / 2 FAIL / 1 INFO / 1 NOT CHECKED`** offline and **`17 PASS / 2 FAIL / 1 INFO`** online, **fifteen gates and five guards, gate set matching the document** — the runner reads the IDs out of `Step9_docs/4thJ_09_enduseLoads_val.md`, so the row had to be declared there before the gate could be counted anywhere.

🔴 **2. `G9.7` is deliberately NOT listed as must-stay-clean on that perturbation row.** A permanently-`INFO` gate staying clean is **vacuous** — it would pass the row even if the model were deleted. `G9.8` stays the must-stay-clean partner, correctly, the four portions being scale-invariant.

⚪ **3. WHAT THIS ARM IS NOT, AND IT MATTERS FOR THE MANUSCRIPT.** It is a **scale / regression** arm, **never an external validation**. 200 l/day is also `4thJ_step9_trigger.py`'s `--dhw-l-per-day` default, so a pass says the pipeline reproduces **its own stated reference** through disaggregation, the four-event split, the peak-flow arithmetic and the per-dwelling write-out — a real path with real arithmetic and a genuine mutation detector, but **not** evidence that 200 l/day is right for Spanish, British or Italian dwellings. **Nobody in this project has measured that.** 🔴 **No number was invented:** 200 l/day is the figure `RL25` §B10 transcribes from the source and `FINDING 165` quotes back.

🔴 **4. THE STATISTIC WAS CHOSEN IN THE OPEN, AND THE ALTERNATIVE IS RECORDED RATHER THAN BURIED.** Jordan & Vajen's 200 l/day is an **annual average per dwelling** (*"one-family house ⇒ 73 000 litres (= 365 days × 200 l/day)"*), so the commensurable statistic is the **stock mean**, and the emitter targets exactly that. `G9.7` used the median because a population band over *people* is a distributional statement; this band is not. ⚪ The emitted per-dwelling distribution is strongly right-skewed — **16.3 to 645.7 l/day** — and its medians are `174.97 / 175.79 / 195.13`, so **a median arm at this same ±10 % would ship FAIL 2** (`es` −12.5 %, `uk` −12.1 %, `it` −2.4 %). 🔴 **The medians are therefore printed in the gate's own note on every run, whatever the verdict**, so the statistic cannot quietly become the flattering one. Switching the basis to the median is a one-line change and a **band decision**; it is written into the gate docstring, the Step 9 log and §10 of the 11.2 record rather than left to be discovered.

🟢 **5. `G11.18` is DECLARED in `Step11_docs/4thJ_11_stockEndUseLoads_val.md`** and inherits `G9.15`'s basis and tolerance unchanged, so **the Step 11 runner cannot be authored without scoring it** — that document is what the runner reads. ⚪ **It is the one DHW arm at stock scale that is not vacuous:** unlike `200 / n_members`, the per-dwelling mean is a quantity `N` genuinely sharpens. `G11.7` stays `INFO` and must be *reported* as such, never as PASS.

🔴 **6. THE TRANSFERABLE LESSON, AND IT IS NOT ABOUT WATER.** A gate does **two** jobs — it scores a quantity and it detects a mutation — and a decision that correctly retires the first **silently retires the second**. `D-S11-1` was right and still cost a detector. ⚪ **Before any future gate is reclassified `INFO` — and `G8.7` is already one — ask what its row in the perturbation table was carrying.** That question costs one line.

⚪ **Where it is written.** `tools/4thJ_gates_step9.py` (constants, `g9_15`, the `run()` call), `tools/4thJ_step9_selftest.py` (the registered `CASES` row), `Step9_docs/4thJ_09_enduseLoads_val.md` (STATUS, gate table, perturbation table, shipped board, progress log), `Step11_docs/4thJ_11_stockEndUseLoads_val.md` (`G11.18` row, `D-S11-2` closure, progress log), `Step11_docs/4thJ_11_stockEndUseLoads.md` (§1.3a, work-item row 11.2, progress log), `Step11_docs/docs/2026-08-27_work-item-11.2_G9.7-diagnosis.md` (**new §10**), `4thJ_00_HETUS_LLM_Pipeline.md` §9B. Backups `*.bak_pre_ds112`, each `[ -s ]`-verified before the write, and line endings checked after it (CRLF files stayed CRLF this time). Board republished at the same URL, label `ds11-2-closed-g915`, **103 / 1 / 11 / 115 unchanged** — no card was created, because `D-S11-2` opened and closed inside work item 11.2. Control seen **REFUSED** (`node --check` rc=1), live rc=0, DOM smoke rc=0.

