#### 🟢 **2026-08-27 (evening) — WORK ITEM 11.2 IS DONE AND `G9.7`'s 2–4× HAS A MECHANISM: THE BAND AND THE MODEL COME FROM TWO DIFFERENT PAPERS, AND THE SCORED QUANTITY IS `200 / n_members`.** Record: `Step11_docs/docs/2026-08-27_work-item-11.2_G9.7-diagnosis.md`. Picked up because it was the one item in Steps 10 and 11 needing **no OpenUBEM cell, no GPU and no Speed job** while `1287613` runs. Four read-only checks over the shipped `outputs_step9/` tree and the vendored `jordan_vajen_iea_task26_v2.0_2001.pdf` (md5 `c7c460924ef66588649b2473b706e2b9`). 🔴 **`FINDING 163` — the band was NEVER Jordan & Vajen's, so its absence from that report was never evidence about the band.** It enters the project at `DeepResearchPrompts/RL13_…` row 15 (2026-08-14, **Tier 2**), which attributes *"30 to 50 L/person/day at 60 deg C"* jointly to Jordan & Vajen **and to Fuentes et al. (2018)**, *A review of domestic hot water consumption profiles…*, **RSER 81(1): 1530–1547, DOI `10.1016/j.rser.2017.05.229`**. §9B of `4thJ_00_HETUS_LLM_Pipeline.md` compressed that row to **one** attribution; Step 9 registered `G9.7` on the compressed sentence, built the model on Jordan & Vajen's table, and cited **only Jordan & Vajen**. **Fuentes is in no citation table in this project.** ⚪ Fuentes has **not been fetched** and its number is **not verified** — `RL13` is Tier 2 and `FINDING 47`'s rule applies. 🔴 **`FINDING 164` — the temperature candidate is REFUTED, not unconfirmed.** The report's Table 1 has **no temperature column at all**, and the paper says outright *"for the cold water temperature distribution during the year, a local profile should be used."* Its only temperature is a **35 K** rise in two worked max-energy examples. ⚪ Granting `RL25`'s unsourced per-category temperatures anyway gives **×0.800**, not §1.3's ×0.600 — bath + shower are exactly **half** the daily volume, not the dominant share — leaving `es` at **80.12**, still outside. 🔴 **`FINDING 165` — `G9.7` measures HOUSEHOLD SIZE,