n byte-identically to the 8.1 artefacts. 🔴 **`G8.1`–`G8.6` all read EXACTLY 0: they are tripwires, not accuracy measurements.** 🔴 **`FINDING 121`: against TABULA's own published `q_h_nd` — an as-modelled reference of the same quantity that `FINDING 44` never examined, covering 86 of 86 codes — the uninjected control sits +136.6 % ABOVE in Spain (21 of 24 cells) and −29.6 % / −36.7 % BELOW in the UK and Italy (32 of 32 each). The sign flips by country: 166 pp, aligned with the LOCO fold, larger than `FINDING 110`/`117`/`120`. Spain's mechanism is MEASURED — TABULA counts a 539-hour heating season, EnergyPlus heats 2,901.** 🔴 `FINDING 122` the simulation timestep is worth −4.1 / +5.6 / −3.7 % and its SIGN DIFFERS BY FOLD; `FINDING 123` EnergyPlus's unruled 18 °C ground default is worth +33.5 / +1.7 / +15.7 %, a 20× country spread; `FINDING 124` one psychrometric warning belongs to the Torino EPW alone — all 32 Italian cells, no others, and the 12/12 weather gate could not have caught it. 🔴 **`FINDING 125` CAPS 8.5: switching `phi_int` off entirely moves heating only +40.5 / +19.7 / +20.1 %, and the sweep only REDISTRIBUTES it, so the “15 to 50 % on annual space heating” the step document quotes is unreachable at the top end in two folds of three.** 🟢 **`D-S8-5` RULED BY THE AUTHOR AND APPLIED THE SAME DAY — NOTHING IS WAITING ON THE AUTHOR IN STEP 8.** Item 1 **(a)**: `G8.7` is **INFO permanently**, no band is ever created (`G87_TOLERANCE_PCT` stays `None`, and selftest `C16` now fails if that changes) — EnergyPlus hourly-dynamic vs TABULA monthly quasi-steady-state is a model-to-model structural comparison, so `FINDING 121` is published as a declared methodological limitation instead of scored. Item 2 **approved**: `D-S8-1`(a) extends **verbatim** to `G8.5`/`G8.6` — reference = the independent re-run, thresholds unmoved, and **the occupancy peak shift is reported as an empirical result, not gated against the flat control** (the `FINDING 44` inversion, now closed in the last two gates it was live in). Re-verified after the change: **`G8.7` INFO = 88, 0 gate-cell FAILs over 88 cells**, selftest **29 ok / 0 FAILED, 12 of 12 injections HIT**; no campaign cell re-run and no measured number changed. ⚪ **Work item 8.4, the two probes, is next and is unblocked.** ⚪ PREVIOUSLY, 2026-08-25 (night): 🟢 `D-S8-4` RULED AND IMPLEMENTED: THE AUTHOR REVERSED THE ACTUAL-YEAR WEATHER RULING, AND WORK ITEM 8.2 IS CLOSED.** The three EPWs are on disk on a **`TMYx.2009-2023`** basis — the same base period for all three folds, and the only published window that contains every original fieldwork period. The station was **selected by measurement**, scoring 44 candidates against TABULA's own published monthly temperatures: `es` **Valencia.Viveros 082850** (0.620), `uk` **Birmingham.AP 035340** (0.533), `it` **Torino.Venaria 160600** (1.043); both planted controls lost. Weather gate **12 ok / 0 FAILED**, **injection battery 9 of 9 seen failing with a clean baseline**. 🔴 **`FINDING 120`: the station is a free parameter worth 5–11 % of heating demand and the UK margin that picked it is 0.002 K** — all 88 archetypes were run twice to measure it (es 10.7 %, uk 5.4 %, it 8.4 % median, and **the sign differs by fold**), so **no cross-fold comparison of absolute demand is safe to ±10 %**; the occupancy effect is untouched because every level of `f` in a fold shares one EPW. 🔴 **`RL27` B12 is falsified and `RL27` has never been vetted at all** — its three named stations are the worst Spanish candidate, a 2.8× worse English one and the worst Italian one. 🔴 `FINDING 118` one climate region with two spellings inside one TABULA release; 🔴 `FINDING 119` TABULA's `HeatingDays` is a MONTHLY-mean statistic and comparing an EPW's daily count to it manufactures a 22-vs-72 artefact. ⚪ The 88 IDFs were rebuilt to clear a now-false `item 8.2 is open` note — **8.1 selftest re-run, 26 ok / 0 FAILED**. ⚪ **Work item 8.3, the uninjected control campaign, is unblocked and is next