until all three land: that is the author's standing instruction of 2026-08-26.

🔴 **The ceiling run's stated blocker was never the real one.** `bitsandbytes` 0.50.1 has
been on Speed since 2026-08-22; what was missing is that **the 8-bit half of the recipe was never
implemented** — the trainer built a plain `torch.optim.AdamW` for every run type, and at 7 B
that is 14 + 14 + **56** = 84 GB before a single activation, on an 80 GB instance. Now implemented,
guarded by `run_type == "ceiling"`, and it **refuses** rather than falling back. ⚪
`envs/step4` stays frozen per `D-S7-3`: bitsandbytes is staged by `pip --target` into
`envs/bnb_for_step4` and put on `PYTHONPATH`. 🔴 **`--no-deps` is load-bearing** — the
first attempt began installing a second CUDA-13 **torch** into that directory, which would have
**shadowed** `envs/step4`'s torch 2.5.1+cu121 and made the ceiling run incomparable to every LoRA
run it exists to be compared against.

