🔴 **`FINDING 99` — applying `D-S7-8` exposed a condition the ruling cannot satisfy alone.** "The
first calendar year of the twelve-month window" gives exact weekend coincidence **only if that window
is January–December**. A straddling window (Jul 2013 – Jun 2014, say) aligns for six months and is off
by one or two weekdays for the rest; a straddling span containing 29 February is **8,784 hours**,
which `year_day_types()` refuses outright; and the emitter has `--year` but **no window-start
parameter**, so a straddling window needs an additive tool change before it can be honoured. ⚪ Needs
no ruling — it is a **constraint on `D-S8-2` item 6**: prefer a calendar-year window, or declare a
partial alignment.

