#### Previously: **2026-08-20 (late night) — 🟢 SECOND ROUND OF RULINGS: `D-S5-3` CLOSED, `FINDING 51` APPLIED, SPAIN'S MICRODATA BASIS RULED. 🔴 `FINDING 52`: THE RAKING ENGINE WAS DELETING DONORS AND REPORTING A PERFECT FIT. 🟢 NEW `Resources/` INDEX OF THE 2J/3J PREPROCESSING PRECEDENTS — READ IT BEFORE ANY PREPROCESSING DECISION.** All three open items were ruled by the author, each as recommended, and all three are applied. **(1) Spain's `strat_age_band` and `strat_sex` STAY on the microdata basis** — `marginals_es.csv` unchanged, md5 `32e1d97d0c107ee8d2eb7034abd18a8a`; the alternative was mixing two universes inside one file. 🔴 **Consequence now RULED not merely recorded: three of Spain's four marginal fields are tables WE tabulated against three of four published aggregates for the UK, so in LOCO — where the held-out country's marginal carries the WHOLE of the null's information — the folds are NOT scored against sources of equal standing. State it wherever a cross-fold `G6.1` margin comparison appears.** **(2) `FINDING 51`: `es` is fitted on FIVE econ bands, `uk` on six** — each fold uses the best marginal its own country publishes. 🔴 **AND IMPLEMENTING THAT SURFACED `FINDING 52`, the sharpest defect of the night: `rake()` builds its IPF factors ONLY from the categories the target names, so a donor carrying a category the target never names hits `factor.get(..., 0.0)` and is MULTIPLIED BY ZERO — not merged, not flagged, DELETED.** Measured on a 120-donor `uk+it` pool against Spain's five bands: **20 of 20 `homemaker` donors zeroed, 16.67 % of the pool gone, `max_dev_pp` = 5.6e-15, NO ERROR RAISED.** 🔴 **The diagnostic reports a flawless fit precisely BECAUSE it converged on the categories that survived** — the sixth was annihilated before the deviation was measured and nothing in the return value shows it; the `es` null would have looked BETTER for having lost a sixth of its donors. ⚪ The engine already guarded the MIRROR image (a target naming a category no do